Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["EMRIs with environment", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002853795031561*^9, 
  4.0028538252429047`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"932ca3a3-1e36-b044-a50e-\
6b09f0ec6026"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Waveform from hybrid approach in vacuum", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002853858212263*^9, 
  4.0028538762620125`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c33f4587-375c-7d48-946d-\
ed624b2f4ed5"],

Cell["\<\
Here, we use the hybrid approach SF+PN introduced by Honet, Pound and Comp\
\[EGrave]re, 2025. to compute waveforms for the inspiral phase in vacuum. The \
goal is to reproduce their main results/ plots. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028538891076775`*^9, 
  4.0028539924706135`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ec350605-1725-a04b-ab49-\
a0e70d07c1d1"],

Cell["In the following, we use the BHPT Teukolsky package:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0045227598315125`*^9, 
  4.004522781678341*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e37eb0fd-9b18-8248-b661-\
1003df0f9775"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"<<", "KerrGeodesics`"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"<<", "Teukolsky`"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0045228101171703`*^9, 4.004522810948717*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"981b2f23-a95e-3c43-8d81-e32796cabc67"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Computation of the energy fluxes", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002854041185013*^9, 4.002854045123495*^9}, {
  4.0028540830281353`*^9, 
  4.0028540913718815`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"150fd680-51d0-7b4e-9052-\
c5e55f781986"],

Cell["\<\
To construct the hybrid energy fluxes, we need to compute the energy fluxes \
at 1 SF (by interpolating from BHPT toolkit data), at 4PN and evaluate the \
common terms. One can then trace the hybrid energy flux. Finally, we will \
compare it to NR data to reproduce the Fig. 9. of the reference paper. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002854105752041*^9, 4.002854127641609*^9}, {
  4.002854176262579*^9, 
  4.0028543489512577`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"65ce85f8-16ee-ad42-99c2-\
a4c03d0ef471"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Energy fluxes in Self-force", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002854382889822*^9, 
  4.002854401973896*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5b9064c0-711b-0d4d-85c0-\
03eaf8cb079d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Evaluate the fluxes at the nodes", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002860884607664*^9, 4.002860885908764*^9}, {
  4.0028643021398907`*^9, 
  4.0028643185551624`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"097e0d52-a65f-d94d-8e50-\
1af8b5c049db"],

Cell["\<\
To compute the energy fluxes at 0PA, one first has to get the data on which \
we can then interpolate. We use the BHPT Teukolsky package:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028608996933556`*^9, 
  4.002860993121992*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4b00a4fc-43c2-774a-8a9c-\
501529bd7e2c"],

Cell["First, we construct the 2D grid of Chebyshev nodes:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028764681074047`*^9, 
  4.002876502246847*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"88902908-2374-8941-8c40-\
174a8cc7461e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nR", " ", "=", " ", "18"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"n\[Chi]", " ", "=", " ", "27"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nodesX", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "i"}], " ", "+", "1"}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", " ", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "nR"}], " ", ")"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"nR", "-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nodesY", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "j"}], " ", "+", "1"}], ")"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", " ", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "n\[Chi]"}], " ", ")"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n\[Chi]", "-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lmax", " ", "=", " ", "5"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Ndigit", " ", "=", " ", "64"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJxTTMoPSmViYGAQBWIQbSKd2Pvw0ltHC81tC0G0gXrkFhDtYX7pAIjO2XX5
CIhmMAo/BqJ7rC3OgeiGhZ5gOiRO/uUjIL1Gwvo1iF6SfJTzMZBeUfUQTL85
yaEPomskdcF0jmuvH4h+0BAUAKL3uPnJPgOZs3eCGojmuKOa9xxI/+hYCKZn
nJ1m+BJIp1yVMALRByJuWoBonlpXSxC949jEKBDtEPgZTN+4+S8eRJsoPkwE
09Lp2SB6zq8PBSC6gr2nEURvsVoNpg0OZL8D0XcMZ4DpJ1e5u18BaR0fnl4Q
vaHNvew1yL1+7OUgOqfl1SHmy0B9GxMPg+gd0+eeBNFTjjadAdEAs4fI+A==

  "],
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7781d88e-d0d9-9841-80fc-c3dfe8c09f2d"],

Cell["\<\
Then, we construct the function giving the energy flux for a point in the \
grid:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002880222232189*^9, 
  4.0028802625960007`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0da558fd-2a91-e043-a721-\
5bc65999e546"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fluxesAtPhasePoint", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rc_", ",", " ", "\[Chi]c_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rp", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"KerrGeoISCO", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\[Chi]c", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "+", "rc"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"e", "=", "0"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"xInc", "=", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"s", "=", 
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"n", "=", "0"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"k", "=", "0"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"orbit", "=", 
         RowBox[{"KerrGeoOrbit", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"N", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[Chi]c", ",", " ", "Ndigit"}], "]"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"N", "[", 
            RowBox[{"rp", ",", " ", "Ndigit"}], "]"}], ",", "e", ",", 
           "xInc"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Total", "[", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"With", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"flux", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"TeukolskyPointParticleMode", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                   "s", ",", " ", "l", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "n", ",", " ",
                     "k", ",", " ", "orbit"}], "]"}], 
                  "[", "\"\<EnergyFlux\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
               "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"flux", "[", "\"\<\[ScriptCapitalI]\>\"", "]"}], ",",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"flux", "[", "\"\<\[ScriptCapitalH]\>\"", "]"}]}], 
                "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ",", 
             "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"l", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "lmax"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "l"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
            "\[IndentingNewLine]", "1"}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
         "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028774308900185`*^9, 4.002877470567009*^9}, 
   4.0028780722820663`*^9, {4.0028781173442936`*^9, 4.0028783144460354`*^9}, {
   4.002878367790333*^9, 4.002878419511427*^9}, {4.0028792291157894`*^9, 
   4.002879287427601*^9}, {4.002879341065695*^9, 4.0028794230666904`*^9}, {
   4.0028794720904694`*^9, 4.002879476421358*^9}, {4.002879664552847*^9, 
   4.0028796689994736`*^9}, {4.002879718255993*^9, 4.0028797266179695`*^9}, {
   4.002879816833212*^9, 4.002879827225025*^9}, {4.0028859472273216`*^9, 
   4.0028859678391094`*^9}, {4.002888406974806*^9, 4.002888415638548*^9}, {
   4.002888954731531*^9, 4.002889006023245*^9}, {4.002889099248049*^9, 
   4.002889115017126*^9}, {4.00289043964056*^9, 4.00289066108877*^9}, {
   4.0028906920656986`*^9, 4.002890755308895*^9}, 4.002892980444416*^9, {
   4.002893153948799*^9, 4.002893189260044*^9}, {4.0028932447853527`*^9, 
   4.0028932624517555`*^9}, {4.002893323499304*^9, 4.0028933437607327`*^9}, {
   4.0028949624544125`*^9, 4.0028949698112335`*^9}, 4.0029520200914345`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4afda8ef-35bd-0e4d-bb2e-6dee3b9bf8b2"],

Cell["\<\
Here, circular equatorial orbit: we can avoid summing on negative m and \
multiply by 2 instead, and the flux vanishes at m=0. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002890889829891*^9, 
  4.0028909888567085`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"150d946f-275f-9641-b9a1-\
bd8fbe69ddfe"],

Cell["Finally, we evaluate the function on the 2D grid:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0028802722651825`*^9, 4.002880273721964*^9}, {
  4.002880426073927*^9, 
  4.002880460460474*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b1eca064-85df-9344-b2d8-\
8b3454b0ad90"],

